  "title": "Discovery Engine: Rollbacks for ToolCall & Collaborative KnowledgeSpace Ops, New Private OAuth & Notebook Scoping",
  "summary": "This update includes significant breaking changes: the recently added `toolCalls.operations.get` and `collaborativeProjects.knowledgeSpaces.operations.get` methods have been removed. Developers should update their integrations. New features include private network OAuth configuration, notebook-level data store scoping, and enhanced field matching options.",
  "details": "This release introduces several breaking changes and significant feature updates. Developers who recently integrated with `projects.locations.collections.engines.assistants.agents.toolCalls.operations.get` (introduced on 2026-10-08) or `projects.locations.collections.engines.collaborativeProjects.knowledgeSpaces.operations.get` (introduced on 2026-09-23) must update their code immediately, as these methods have been removed. Additionally, the newly introduced `projects.locations.knowledgeSpaces.operations.get` method now strictly requires the `name` parameter.\n\nOn the feature front, you can now configure OAuth providers that are only reachable over private networks using the new `privateNetworkConfig` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAuthorizationServerSideOAuth2`. Data stores can be restricted to specific notebooks via the new `notebooks` array in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreFederatedSearchConfigNotebooklmConfig` (also available in V1 and V1beta). Fine-tune search behavior with new `partialMatchableOption` and `prefixMatchableOption` fields in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFieldConfig`. Feedback mechanisms are enhanced with `GOOGLE_AGENTSPACE_DESKTOP` as a `feedbackSource` and new `stepSeqNum`, `trajectoryId` fields in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFeedbackConversationInfo`. Minor updates include clarified descriptions for the `GRACE_PERIOD` state in license configurations.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
